scoswm (0.4.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the desktop wallpaper pixmap: the gradient and grid were still
    painted onto the root window and then covered by the pixmap copy,
    which hid the grid lines and kept the desktop flickering.
  * Make the mouse wheel work on WM surfaces: it scrolls the launcher
    list (previously the offset snapped back to the selection) and
    cycles windows on the desktop and taskbar.
  * Add hover highlighting on desktop icons, taskbar items and window
    title buttons, pressed/starting feedback on taskbar pins, and
    clear a desktop icon's selection as soon as empty desktop is
    clicked.
  * Define the themed arrow cursor on the root window, WM chrome and
    window frames so the pointer no longer changes style between
    applications and the desktop.
  * Reachable resize zones on every window edge and corner (from the
    client area too, not just the 1 px frame), and dragging a
    maximised window's titlebar restores it under the pointer.
  * Short minimise/restore transitions so windows no longer appear
    and vanish instantaneously.

 -- Joe <167563398+Joercat@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400

scoswm (0.4.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix leaked drag state: a button release now ends any drag wherever
    it lands. Releasing over another window or the taskbar previously
    left windows glued to the pointer, suppressed desktop repaints and
    left ghost frames of closed windows on the desktop.
  * Paint the wallpaper into a root background pixmap so the X server
    restores the desktop instantly when windows close/move (no more
    split-second flicker or leftover window outlines).
  * Discover apps in all XDG data dirs plus Flatpak and Snap export
    directories, and add an "All installed apps..." browse mode to
    the launcher (Esc returns to the core view).

 -- Joe <167563398+Joercat@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:00:00 -0400

scoswm (0.4.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Log session starts, WM messages and exit status to
    ~/.cache/scoswm/session.log in scoswm-session, so a failed SDDM
    login leaves a readable reason instead of a silent flash.
  * Silence -Wformat-truncation build warnings (bounded copies) so
    real build errors are visible; the warnings were harmless.
  * More X core font fallbacks and a clear log line if the X server
    connection is lost mid-session.

 -- Joe <167563398+Joercat@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0400

scoswm (0.4.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add Debian packaging (debian/) and a quick packaging/build-deb.sh
    so the window manager builds and installs natively on Debian.
  * Harden the SDDM/X11 session entry: TryExec now names the
    scoswm-session entry point, so SDDM only lists SCosWM when the
    session launcher is actually installed and executable.
  * Detect Debian's x-terminal-emulator alternative (and pcmanfm-qt /
    caja / mate-terminal) when choosing the default terminal and file
    manager.
  * Session launcher exports sensible XDG session variables for
    startx/xinit use; under SDDM these are already provided.

 -- Joe <167563398+Joercat@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400

